**Haryana** is among the richest states but has the lowest sex ratio. In all big states, males outnumber females among people aged 7 and above.

@section 24.2 | Child Sex Ratio

@q 16:127-134

@table
Child sex ratio (0-6 years) | Figure
India | **1961: 976** → 1991: 945 → 2001: 927 → **2011: 918** (provisional 914); **falling continuously**
Highest (2011) | **Mizoram (970)**, **Meghalaya (970)**, Chhattisgarh (969)
Lowest (2011) | **Haryana (834)**, Punjab (846), J&K (862)
Haryana | Rose from 819 (2001) to 834 (2011)
Causes of low sex ratio | **Female foeticide**, higher **girl-child deaths**, **maternal deaths**, more boys born
@end

**Rural** sex ratio (949) is higher than **urban** (929), and **female infant mortality** is higher than male in India, so statement (iv) in Q134 is false.

