Kerala's high literacy comes from early **social reform, schools and public policy**, not mainly from its Christian population.

@section 24.4 | Population Policy and Fertility

@q 16:145-147

@src1 16:17
@one U.P. Lower Sub. (Pre) 2002
As per the National Population Policy 2000, the birth rate has to be reduced by the year 2010 to
@ans 21 per 1000
@end

@table
National Population Policy 2000 | Detail
Announced | **15 February 2000**
Goals | TFR to **replacement level (2.1) by 2010**; **stable population by 2045**, later pushed to **2070**
Other aims | Free, compulsory schooling to 14; IMR below 30; MMR below 100; **registration of births, deaths, marriages, pregnancies**; role for **SHGs** and panchayats
National Commission on Population | Chaired by the **Prime Minister** (2000)
@end

